  "details": "I hope people don't actually upload any new SDK2 avatar content anymore, but existing content is out there and is using said system.\n\nThis is the most popular tool, which generated those toggle systems: https://github.com/Xiexe/VRCInventorySystem-DEPREACTED---USE-AVATARS-3.0-\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Open the VRChat Open beta on Unity 2022 in VR\n\n2. Switch to an SDK2 Avatar with toggles (here is one of mine, which exhibits the issue: `avtr_fc8e07ab-b0e1-4cfa-ade2-2c975267e0aa`, its lightsaber and smartphone toggles work on live, but are broken on beta in VR)\n\n3. Try to use said toggles (other people in the lobby should be able to see the issue too, provided they are on the beta and in VR)\n\n## Possible Solutions\n\n1. Find why those systems are breaking and fix the issue in the client\n\n2. Block SDK2 uploads (optional) and server side migrate SDK2 content and the toggle systems to SDK3, that would mean somehow loading the old assetbundles, altering them and repacking them. I am not sure unity has some way to do that properly, it may require cursed code to do.\n\n3. ~~Ignore the problem and pretend SDK2 content doesn't exist~~",
